Vendored third-party dependency, moved to soroban-sdk 29
========================================================

  Library:  soroban-sdk-tools 0.1.4 (Rust, no_std)
  Upstream: https://github.com/BlaineHeffron/soroban-sdk-tools
  Release:  crates.io soroban-sdk-tools 0.1.4 (.crate sha256
            1ac9ff2d918e0ca97ee7b29f887192afe157c95ecb0a4db94f6811ae8de682fe),
            published from commit 2143316cbd325ff9c76e1720bfe47fbe29627a8e
            ("chore: release v0.1.4 (#43)"), path soroban-sdk-tools
  License:  Apache-2.0 (see LICENSE)
  Used by:  perch-smart-account, perch-doc-compiler,
            perch-recovery-interface, perch-recovery, perch-zk-pool,
            perch-testnet (`scerr`, typed storage)

Why vendored
------------
soroban-sdk-tools 0.1.4, its newest release, requires soroban-sdk ^28, and
no upstream branch moves it to 29 (checked 2026-11-03). Perch builds with
soroban-sdk 29.0.1 / soroban-env-host 29.0.1, and a crate that requires
another soroban-sdk major cannot share its types, so this copy is built as a
path dependency with the soroban-sdk pin moved. No change was proposed
upstream.

Upstream files
--------------
Every file is upstream's bytes except Cargo.toml (the published, normalized
manifest), whose delta is below. UPSTREAM.sha256 lists the sha256 of every
vendored file as published, with LICENSE taken from the repository root at
the commit above (the published crate carries none).

Not vendored: tests/, Cargo.lock, Cargo.toml.orig. The proc-macro crate it
depends on, soroban-sdk-tools-macro 0.1.4, stays on crates.io: it links no
soroban-sdk (its soroban-spec 28 and stellar-xdr =28.0.0 are build-time
only, and stellar-xdr 28.0.0 is the version soroban-sdk 29 uses).

SDK 29 delta
------------
Cargo.toml only:

  - `[dependencies.soroban-sdk]` version "28.0.0" became "29.0.1";
  - the `[dev-dependencies]` table and the `[[test]]` targets were dropped
    (the tests are not vendored).

The source builds unchanged: soroban-sdk 29 has no API changes from 28
(soroban-sdk's own migration notes: "Migrating from v28 to v29: None").

Updating
--------
Replace the directory with the new upstream files, re-apply the delta above,
regenerate UPSTREAM.sha256 from the unmodified upstream files, and update
this NOTICE. crates/integration-tests/tests/vendor.rs requires every
vendored file other than Cargo.toml to hash to UPSTREAM.sha256 (after
reversing any source delta above) and the directory to hold nothing else but
NOTICE and UPSTREAM.sha256, so no other upstream byte can change unnoticed.
